  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSAN - core funding for the advocacy and public affairs work of the national team</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	CSAN is seeking support for core funding for the advocacy and public affairs work of the national team. This team, based in Romero House, Southwark, is the supportive centre and development engine of a network of charities and Catholic Dioceses whose work is founded in the precepts of Catholic Social Teaching (CST).
2.	The network has 42 members and is growing. It works in domestic social action and seeks social justice, recognising that the need for our services and our public voice of advocacy is urgent at this time.
3.	The cost of the advocacy, lobbying and campaign work of the CSAN team is some &#xa3;70,000 per annum. A grant of that amount to cover this core work of CSAN is being sought from CAFOD. It is notable that this work is lending itself ever better and more persuasively to effective lobbying and campaigning in solidarity with CAFOD &#x2013; examples being the joint general election campaign and the prospective refugee campaign in 2016.</narrative>
  </description>
